 1  B
 NH2 + photon = NH + H
!
! photoabsorption cross section and photodissociation yield from Leiden database (Hrodmarsson & van Dishoeck 2023, A&A, 675, A25, https://home.strw.leidenuniv.nl/~ewine/photo/)
! same than section adopted by Agundez et al 2018, A&A, 616, A19 (based on digitizing figures 8, 11, and 12 of Koch 1997, J Phys Chem A, 101, 1460) except for an additional intense band assumed at 110.2 nm (see arguments in Heays et al 2017, A&A, 602, A105)
!
! Two photodissociation channels are possible:
! NH2 + photon -> NH + H (a)
!              -> N + H2 (b)
! channel (a) is the major one (see experimental evidence in Biehl et al 1994, and theoretical evidence in Vetter et al 1996)
!
! photodissociation threshold for channel (a) is 300 nm (Huebner et al 1992)
! photoionization   threshold                 is 113 nm
!
! sigma is the total photoabsorption cross section
! yield is the photodissociation yield relative to photoabsorption
!
! wlth[nm]  sigma[cm2]   yield(s)...
